{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1529360-the-immaculate-foundation-scp-meets-exalted-shard","id":1529360,"title":"The Immaculate Foundation [SCP meets Exalted Shard]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-24T15:56:00-08:00","id":1529360,"title":"The Immaculate Foundation [SCP meets Exalted Shard]","content":"So this is something that came up in the Exalted Discord which I thought to bring up here while I'm working on my main Apocryphal Setting Shard.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea came from how the Immaculate Order does, do a degree, has some similarities with the SCP Foundation in terms of fighting and containing certain supernatural threats, with the Jade Prison breaking being a full blown Keter Containment Breach. So, I thought about playing around with the idea, or at least putting it here to see what people think about it. With that in mind, this is the rough idea-<br /> <br /> Here is the Immaculate Foundation- the last line of defense to maintain the peace in modern society. Standing in the shadows of history with an unclear origin, the Immaculate Order is a global organization dedicated towards stopping the world from descending into chaos. This chaos is the result of the so called XSs (shortcut for Exalted Essences. Yeah, original name, but let's work with that). Each XS is defined for its ability to create XS-C (stands for &quot;Chosen&quot;), which are anomalous people who draw upon great, unregulated power that might undermine the very structure of society. As such, when a new XS-C emerges, is requires sending a WYLD hunting unit in order to either contain or neutralize the threat. However, the Foundation sees containment of the XS as a better, preemptive measure, as it allows to stop the creation of new XS-Cs. XSs are themselves being divided into three main categories- Safe, Inauspicious and Anathema, depending on how hard it is to contain XS-Cs, and each requires a certain protocol to contain them. While most XSs manifest themselves in human beings, there is a section known as XS-R which takes the form of full blown anomalous beings, where containment requires dealing with alien species which are hostile towards human society. Other beings are XS-P, which are potential XSs which are yet to actually become an XS, but are in a danger to do, often taking the form of anomalous beings of great power. The Foundation itself, obviously, is <i>not</i> made out of XS-Cs, does not rely on anomalous power, and does not have a shadow council which has a specific agenda in tries to pushes. Don't be absurd- those are lies sprouted by its rivals, such as SILVER and the Illuminated Heresy. Also, the intentions of the XS-Cs are not a consideration for the Foundation's behavior- so in case you become an XS-C, you should be understanding and cooperate with WYLD during the containment process. It is for the greater good, after all. <br /> <br /> So, with this in mind, let's just have fun and put here a list of potential XSs the Immaculate Foundation needs to deal with. <br /> <br /> XS-001: The Jade Prison (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-002: The Scarlet Empress (Safe). Subdivided into XS-002-1 (Earth Dragon Bloodline), XS-002-2 (Air Dragon Bloodline), XS-002-3 (Wood Dragon Bloodline), XS-002-4 (Fire Dragon Bloodline) and XS-002-5 (Water Dragon Bloodline).<br /> <br /> XS-003: the Loom of Fate (Safe). Subdivided into XS-003-1 (Omen of Journeys), XS-003-2 (Omen of Serenity), XS-003-3 (Omen of Battles), XS-003-4 (Omen of Secrets) and XS-003-4 (Omen of Endings)<br /> <br /> XS-004: the Lunar Dominion (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-005: the Monstrance of Celestial Portion (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-006: the Gate of Eight Divinities (Inauspicious)<br /> <br /> XS-007: the Chrysalis Grotesque (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-008: the Dark Mother (Inauspicious)<br /> <br /> XS-009: the Fallen Paradise (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-010: the Trench (Safe)<br /> <br /> XS-011: the Dream (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-012: the Penumbra (Inauspicious)<br /> <br /> XS-013: the Opal Shrine (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-014: the Grimscythe (Inauspicious)<br /> <br /> XS-015: the Infrastructure (Safe)<br /> <br /> XS-016: the Puppet Theater (Anathema)<br /> <br /> XS-017: the Font of Glories (Inauspicious)<br /> <br /> (obviously there is a bunch more we could add to here, but this is a starting point I guess- feel free to through your own ideas on how to tackle this subject/develop current XSs/add new ones!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}